Governance/enforcement-only successor after merged postmerge carrier #395.

Exact predecessor main: `1fc857881937ad357a6f5aadd127739c969e953e`.

Material delta:
- separates `QIKVRT requested review execution` from `QIKVRT required code-owner review`;
- requires the native rule to carry both `test` and `QIKVRT required code-owner review`;
- defines the Mirror main-ruleset policy;
- adds a fail-closed create/reconcile/readback workflow for that native ruleset;
- adds tests for the required status-check condition.

Explicitly unchanged:
- Charter bytes;
- postmerge readback carrier content;
- predecessor evidence;
- publication state.

No bot comment is treated as a native approval. No merge, publication, FINAL_PASS or EFFECT_ACK_DONE is claimed.

Implements the owner-authorized repository PR closure engine.

Scope:
- scan up to 8 oldest open main-base PRs per run;
- apply at most one repository mutation per run;
- close only already-contained PRs without evidence transfer;
- advance trusted self-heal drafts, update stale same-repository branches, and request current independent review;
- merge only after fresh exact-head required check, technical review status, and exact-head independent Goldkelch approval;
- Authority promotion remains behind active ruleset 19344903 and its strict native `test` check;
- Mirror promotion uses an unforced fast-forward ref update as a current-main CAS.

Hard boundaries:
- PREDECESSOR_EVIDENCE_TRANSFER=false
- no self-review as independent review
- no force push
- no Zenodo/IETF/release mutation
- no fabricated PASS, FINAL_PASS, or EFFECT_ACK_DONE

Focused local decision-core regression suite: 12/12 PASS. This is not a repository-wide PASS claim.

The existing repository-evidence materialization path remains responsible for the canonical integrity trio on the exact PR head.

Persists the exact NDR/DSN requirements carrier and its verification boundary without promoting byte identity into implementation, acceptance, end-to-end, or effect evidence.

Current scope:
- exact 25,361-byte carrier at `source/NDR_DSN_ACCEPTANCE_DELTA_V1.json`, SHA-256 `936686c7b6c1e249e8b31215d5111b76a78e494d0ea822a505bd309f946e278e`;
- machine-readable identity/status receipt at `evidence/requirements/NDR_DSN_ACCEPTANCE_DELTA_V1.identity-status.json`, SHA-256 `ae21fe8f28e9e7e077ea0d1a77b161274c1bd8b88e50d599fce316732eb992f7`;
- IETF next-submission scope and evidence-scope threat model, explicitly delta-checked against active revision -03;
- hash-bound Zenodo publication draft at `release/ndr-dsn-requirements-carrier-zenodo-v1/PUBLISH_REQUEST_DRAFT.json`, SHA-256 `9bfca71dfdd1dfa9d9e4b30aeda334fddcc583da56f79cc388aa92ae09abe36c`.

The Zenodo draft is intentionally non-executable until fresh exact-head gates, current independent review, legitimate merge, exact-main readback, executable machine proof/manifest binding, token-bearing publication, and public Zenodo file-hash readback are established.

No Zenodo or IETF external mutation is claimed by this PR. IMPLEMENTATION_VERIFIED, ACCEPTANCE_TESTS_EXECUTED, END_TO_END_VALIDATED, and EFFECT_ACK_DONE remain false.

